---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import GovernAuthorizeVerify from "../components/diagrams/GovernAuthorizeVerify.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Platform | BeaconGuard Govern, Authorize, Verify"
  description="BeaconGuard provides Govern, Authorize, and Verify for regulated AI actions: Active Verified Releases, Request Admission Authorization, Result-to-Action Authorization, and read-only verification."
>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <h1>Platform product map</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      BeaconGuard is structured as three functional domains: Govern, Authorize,
      and Verify. It governs whether an enterprise application may invoke an AI
      provider and whether a declared enterprise action based on an AI-generated
      result may proceed. Provider success is not enterprise authorization.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Govern · Authorize · Verify</h2>
    <p>
      Use this product map to orient. Technical depth lives in documentation.
    </p>
    <GovernAuthorizeVerify />
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Govern</h2>
    <ul class="platform-map-list">
      <li>Compliance Playbooks</li>
      <li>Validation</li>
      <li>Approval</li>
      <li>Signing</li>
      <li>Distribution</li>
      <li>Active Verified Release</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Govern builds and activates the control set. Distribution alone does not
      activate a release.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/docs/policy-model">Policy model documentation</a>
      ·
      <a href="/docs/deployment-integration">Deployment and integration</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Authorize</h2>
    <ul class="platform-map-list">
      <li>Request Admission Authorization</li>
      <li>Untrusted AI-generated result</li>
      <li>Declared action</li>
      <li>Result-to-Action Authorization</li>
      <li>Binary ALLOW or DENY</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Authorize returns binary ALLOW or DENY at request admission and at the
      declared intended action. Review does not convert a recorded DENY into
      ALLOW.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/how-it-works">How It Works</a>
      ·
      <a href="/canonical-workflow">Canonical Workflow</a>
      ·
      <a href="/docs/enforcement-runtime">Enforcement runtime</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Verify</h2>
    <ul class="platform-map-list">
      <li>Executive Reporting</li>
      <li>Decision Explorer</li>
      <li>Deterministic Reconstruction</li>
      <li>Source Evidence</li>
      <li>Replay Verification</li>
      <li>Verifiable Export</li>
      <li>Non-authoritative AI-assisted insights</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Verify is read-only. It cannot grant runtime authority, mutate historical
      decisions, or authorize enterprise actions. AI-assisted insights are not
      part of the trusted authorization path.
    </p>
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/verification">Explore Verification</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/proof-evidence">Proof and Evidence</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Existing systems remain in place</h2>
    <p>
      BeaconGuard does not replace the system of record, workflow application,
      EHR, AML system, fraud system, SIEM, IAM, or GRC tool. BeaconGuard
      authorizes; the enterprise application executes; the enterprise system of
      record remains authoritative.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Priority regulated workflows</h2>
    <div class="section-grid section-grid--compact">
      <div class="content-card">
        <h3>Healthcare</h3>
        <p>PHI-sensitive operational AI workflows.</p>
        <p><a href="/healthcare">Healthcare workflows</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-card">
        <h3>Financial Services</h3>
        <p>AML, KYC, fraud, dispute, and recommendation workflows.</p>
        <p><a href="/fintech">Financial workflows</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-card">
        <h3>Regulated automation</h3>
        <p>Fail-closed authorization before enterprise effect.</p>
        <p><a href="/canonical-workflow">Canonical workflow</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Technical documentation</h2>
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/docs/architecture">Architecture</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/docs/enforcement-runtime">Enforcement runtime</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/docs/compliance-audit">Compliance and audit</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/security">Security</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
